# XCU prs
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# SCCS files are made and inspected only with the SCCS utilities (admin,
# get, delta, prs and friends); the file format is unspecified so nothing
# reads the files directly. A missing companion utility makes the test
# UNRESOLVED. Login names, dates and the diagnostic texts are never compared
# literally.

assertion  XCU.prs.001
anchor     utilities/prs.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/prs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       With no -r, prs writes the SCCS pathname and then, for each
           delta, the delta line, line statistics, MR and comment headings.
test       t/001-default-output.sh

assertion  XCU.prs.002
anchor     utilities/prs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       The keywords :I: :R: :L: :B: :S: :DT: :Li: :Ld: :Lu: :DS: :DP:
           :M: :F: :Z: :W: :D: :T: and their parts give the stored values;
           \t and \n in the data specification are a tab and a newline.
test       t/002-data-keywords.sh

assertion  XCU.prs.003
anchor     utilities/prs.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       -r picks one delta (the latest with no SID), -e adds all earlier
           ones and -l all later ones, and a cutoff before every delta with
           -e selects nothing.
test       t/003-select-deltas.sh

assertion  XCU.prs.004
anchor     utilities/prs.html#STDOUT
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       :C: gives the comment given to delta and :P: is not empty.
test       t/004-comments.sh

assertion  XCU.prs.005
anchor     utilities/prs.html#OPTIONS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       Without -a only existing deltas are shown; with -a a removed
           delta is shown with type R.
test       t/005-removed-deltas.sh

assertion  XCU.prs.006
anchor     utilities/prs.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/prs.html#STDIN
anchor     utilities/prs.html#EXIT STATUS
class      conditional
when       XSI
since      1992
says       A directory operand processes each SCCS file in it and ignores
           other files, a - operand reads names from standard input, and a
           missing file gives a non-zero status.
test       t/006-operands.sh
